Z||000000||Philphine||11-04-2001||08:57 PM||||<BR>late eighties 4.5 caddies pop up at the disabled veterans donation lot off and on and i'm just wondering if they might also be a good sourse for brake pieces for going to a 4.5 (115mm) bolt pattern. if so what years? what if any other parts might be scavenged off a caddy to make getting a whole one more worth it? <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||11-04-2001||11:07 PM||||I used late model Pontiac 6000 full sized spindles and calipers with my Northstar conversion (I believe there is light duty and full size).  They fit right into the Alante hubs and also had the 5X115 bolt pattern.  I know the Alante hubs I used had the Northstar but it may be the same axles/hubs on the 4.x series as well.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
